Anime-style wide illustration, clean line art, soft cel shading, gentle natural colours, cinematic composition, no text, no letters, no readable marks. Reference 1 is Adler Crane, a broad-shouldered man of about forty-five, olive-pale skin, short brown hair going grey at the sides, square jaw, tired brown eyes, in a plain dark close-fitting high-necked security jacket. Reference 2 is a surveyor, a lean man of about thirty-eight with pale light skin and short messy black hair, dark brown eyes, in a plain dark grey surveyor's work jacket and trousers, no scars, no marks on his neck; his two wrists are held together in front of him bound by a white plastic cable tie. Reference 3 is a survey ship control hall at night. Night, above water, on the open deck of a survey ship: Crane walks the surveyor along a long steel rail above deep black water, one hand on the surveyor's arm, the surveyor walking in front with his head up and a stunned calm face. The lit control hall glows warm behind them through its windows. Dark sea, a few stars. Exactly two people, nobody else on the deck. Eyes fully drawn with irises, pupils and highlights.
